    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3426, Ins L (as proposed in S.4326 & A.5379)",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7768\n\nSPONSOR: BRESLIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law, in relation to providing for a policy\nterm of less than one year in certain situations\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2021,\nc.679, to clarify provisions relating to consumer protections when an\ninsurer grants a policy term of less than one year.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter with technical changes\nthat strengthen consumer protections.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 69 of 2021, this legislation is a negotiated\nchange to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 679 of the Laws of 2021. S.4326 and A.5379\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in April 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2021 amending the insurance law relating to\nproviding for a policy term of less than one year in certain situations,\nas proposed in legislative bills numbers S.4326 and A.5379, takes\neffect.  113\n",
